\": \"<Respond to the Question 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nGreg was raised in a conservative family. Therefore, Greg did not have much freedom in selecting jobs and applied for a job that could satisfy his family's requirements but not his own. When the decision letter came out, he was rejected by the company and they wished him the best of luck. He sighed.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Greg ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Admiration\nB) Embarrassment\nC) Anger\nD) Hopeless\nE) Guilt\nF) Relief\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Greg feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) He was afraid of disappointing his family\nB) He was worried about the responsibilities of the job\nC) He was rejected from a job he didn't like\nD) He was worried about the upcoming job interview","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.008577487251125584,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af5a5e99aa9dc5a833d954c","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794483689401,"createTime":"2026-11-12 19:41:29","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"e491fec833dd48cfbcad0d9507aadcb1"}